{
  "title": "Imam Husayn (a.s.)'s Dua in Prayers",
  "data": "Imam al-Husayn (a.s.) is reported to have said this supplicatory prayer in the second unit of his ritual prayers (in the qunut):\nاَللّٰهُمَّ مَنْ اٰوٰى اِلٰى مَاْوًى فَاَنْتَ مَاْوَاىَ وَمَنْ لَجَاَ اِلٰى مَلْجَاٍ فَاَنْتَ مَلْجَئِىْ\nALLAAHUMMA MAN AAWAA ILAA MA'WAN FA-ANTA MA'WAAYA WA MAN LAJA'A ILAA MALJA'IN FA-ANTA MALJA'EE\nO Allah, whoever takes shelter in a shelter, You are my shelter; and whoever takes refuge in a refuge, You are my refuge.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ وَاسْمَعْ نِدَاۤئِىْ وَاَجِبْ دُعَاۤئِىْ وَاجْعَلْ مَاٰبِىْ عِنْدَكَ وَمَثْوَاىَ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMADIN WASMA' NIDAA'EE WA AJIB DU'AA'EE WAJ'AL MA'AABEE I'NDAKA WA MATHWAAY\nO Allah, bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad, hear my call, answer my supplication, and make my return and my abode with You.\nوَاحْرُسْنِىْ فِىْ بَلْوَاىَ مِنِ افْتِتَانِ الْاِمْتِحَانِ وَلَمَّةِ الشَّيْطَانِ\nWAHRUSNEE FEE BALWAAYA MINIF TITAANIL IMTIHAANI WA LAMMATISH SHAYTAAN\nGuard me in my trials from being led astray by the test and from the touch of Satan,\nبِعَظَمَتِكَ الَّتِىْ لَا يَشُوْبُهَا وَلَعُ نَفْسٍ بِتَفْتِيْنٍ وَلَا وَارِدُ طَيْفٍ بِتَظْنِيْنٍ وَلَا يَلُمُّ بِهَا فَرَحٌ\nBI-A'ZAMATIKAL LATEE LAA YASHOOBUHAA WA LA'U NAFSIN BITAFTEENIN WA LAA WAARIDU TAYFIN BITAZNEENIN WA LAA YALUMMU BIHAA FARAH\nby Your greatness, which no soul's craving taints with temptation, no passing phantom with suspicion, and which no (vain) joy comes near,\nحَتّٰى تَقْلِبَنِىْ اِلَيْكَ بِاِرَادَتِكَ غَيْرَ ظَنِيْنٍ وَلَا مَظْنُوْنٍ وَلَا مُرَابٍ وَلَا مُرْتَابٍ اِنَّكَ اَرْحَمُ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nHATTAA TAQLIBANEE ILAYKA BI-IRAADATIKA GHAYRA ZANEENIN WA LAA MAZNOONIN WA LAA MURAABIN WA LAA MURTAABIN INNAKA ARHAMUR RAAHIMEEN\nuntil You turn me back to You by Your will, neither suspicious nor suspected, neither doubted nor doubting. Surely You are the Most Merciful of the merciful.\nIn his book Muhaj al-Da'awat, Sayyid Ibn Tawus has compiled the supplications of the Holy Imams (a.s.) in their ritual prayers (i.e. in the qunut). However, to avoid length, the author of al-Baqiyat al-Salihat has mentioned only the supplication above."
}
